  3.974832148617345*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9b4efac7-dd96-499b-a7a1-\
b2d81fc82056"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Since we have three MB integrals and each one has four series solutions, we \
obtain a total of ",
 StyleBox["12",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " series. To recover the final solution of the original MB integral, we must \
",
 StyleBox["group",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " these series correctly according to their regions of convergence. In this \
simple case, we can do this straightforwardly by inspecting the ",
 StyleBox["master",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " series characteristic lists."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.832764026836339*^9, 3.832764114039603*^9}, {
  3.8327643856316204`*^9, 3.8327644223587313`*^9}, {3.8328235614916153`*^9, 
